2. Backend Module
This will handle all the API logic, database interactions, authentication, and authorization.

Directory Structure:
/controllers: Responsible for handling the incoming HTTP requests (routes for admin, company, and employee functionalities).
/services: Business logic that communicates between controllers and models. For example, handling user management, data fetching, etc.
/models: Contains the data models for things like users, permissions, audio tracks, playlists, etc.
/repositories: Interfaces with the database (e.g., interacting with the Spotify API or your custom DB).
/config: Configuration files (e.g., for environment variables, API keys, etc.).
/utils: Helper functions, custom exceptions, and utility methods.
