Define User Stories & Features (based on the app's major functionalities)

2. Music Service Integration
Integrate Music APIs (Spotify/Napster):
API key setup
Authentication (OAuth2 for Spotify or other methods for Napster)
Fetching songs, playlists, and metadata (e.g., explicit content flags)
Playlist management (creating, modifying, and playing)

3. Backend System Design
Design and Implement Backend (Java Spring Boot or similar):
User Authentication (QR code-based login)
Location-based Account Management (assigning and managing accounts per location)
Playlist Management (storing, rotating playlists, and pulling from music API)
Audio Message Management (uploading and scheduling audio messages)
Song Selection & Employee Input Handling (voting, flagging songs, adding to playlists)
Database Design (storing user data, playlists, song selections, etc.)

4. Frontend Development (User Interface)
Employee Login Screen (QR code login and first-time setup)
Song Search & Selection Interface (search for songs, display alternatives for flagged content)
Playlist Display and Controls (show current playlist, allow song skipping or requesting new songs)
Audio Message Display (listening to corporate messages between songs)
User Feedback Mechanisms (song flagging, feedback on content)

5. Audio Message Management
Upload & Store Audio Messages (for HR guidelines, company-wide messages)
Message Scheduling & Timing (insert messages at specific intervals between songs)
Message Format (how messages are structured and played)

6. Shift-Specific Playlist Management
Shift-Based Playlist Creation (define playlists for each shift based on employee input)
Playlist Rotation & Overlap (manage timing for smooth transitions between shifts)
Song Pool Management (allow employees to add songs to a shared pool and ensure only non-explicit content)

7. Admin Dashboard
Monitor Playlists & Song Selections (view and adjust location-specific playlists)
Insert Corporate Messages (add and schedule HR guidelines and location-specific messages)
Analytics & Reporting (track employee song selections, flagging behavior, and message engagement)

8. Testing and QA
Unit Testing (test individual components like song fetching, playlist rotation, and message scheduling)
Integration Testing (ensure everything works together, from song selection to message insertion)
User Testing (test the interface with real users to ensure it’s intuitive)

9. Deployment & Maintenance
Set Up Deployment Pipeline (for both backend and frontend, e.g., using Docker, Kubernetes)
Deploy App to Production (on a cloud platform like AWS, Heroku, etc.)
Monitoring & Bug Fixing (set up logging, track errors, and update the app based on user feedback)
This list should give you a roadmap for your app development. Each task can be broken down into smaller, manageable pieces. Focus on one area at a time, and don’t hesitate to ask for specific guidance as you move forward. You're well on your way!
